  <!-- THE WORKFLOW, WRITTEN DOWN: TILE CHAIN WITH ANIMATED CONNECTORS -->
  <section class="workflow-steps-section" id="workflow-steps">
    <div class="wf-steps-container">

      <div class="wf-steps-header">
        <span class="wf-steps-eyebrow">The workflow, written down</span>
        <h2 class="wf-steps-title">
          <!-- The desktop line jokes about not playing with the interactive
               desktop, which mobile cannot reach at all. Each gets its own. -->
          <span class="wf-title-desktop">
            If you don't want to play with the cool interactive desktop, I guess you
            can read this instead <span class="wf-cough">*cough*</span> boring
            <span class="wf-cough">*cough*</span>
          </span>
          <span class="wf-title-mobile">
            Each step returns hours of time to my hands
          </span>
        </h2>
      </div>

      <ol class="wf-chain">
        <li class="wf-node" style="--wf-accent: var(--doodle-yellow, #FFDA00); --wf-ink: #000000;">
          <div class="wf-node-card">
            <div class="wf-node-top">
              <span class="wf-step-num">01</span>
              <span class="wf-node-tag">AUTOMATED SCAN &middot; CRON</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="wf-node-title">Scanning for new job postings</h3>
            <p class="wf-node-lead">An automated schedule scans online job boards three times a day to find newly listed jobs that fit my target criteria.</p>
            <button class="wf-expand-btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="wf-detail-01">
              <span class="wf-expand-label">Read the techy details</span>
              <span class="wf-chevron" aria-hidden="true">&#9662;</span>
            </button>
            <div class="wf-detail" id="wf-detail-01" hidden>
              <p class="wf-detail-p">The OpenClaw Gateway daemon runs in the background 24/7. Three times a day (09:00, 13:00, 18:00 BST), its built-in scheduler spins up an isolated, ephemeral container. It triggers <code>runner.py</code> to execute a delta scrape based on the last recorded timestamp, parsing and normalizing listings into structured JSON without lingering background state.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <span class="wf-connector" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </li>
        <li class="wf-node" style="--wf-accent: var(--doodle-lime, #D1FF00); --wf-ink: #000000;">
          <div class="wf-node-card">
            <div class="wf-node-top">
              <span class="wf-step-num">02</span>
              <span class="wf-node-tag">PYTHON FILTER &middot; ZERO AI COST</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="wf-node-title">Filtering out irrelevant listings</h3>
            <p class="wf-node-lead">A fast sorting script grades every job on title, seniority, location, and salary floors to immediately toss out spam, low pay, and bad fits.</p>
            <button class="wf-expand-btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="wf-detail-02">
              <span class="wf-expand-label">Read the techy details</span>
              <span class="wf-chevron" aria-hidden="true">&#9662;</span>
            </button>
            <div class="wf-detail" id="wf-detail-02" hidden>
              <p class="wf-detail-p"><code>scorer.py</code> checks incoming data against a local SQLite database to prevent duplicates. It runs deterministic Python regex pattern matching and scoring matrices without making any AI model calls. Listings that meet the minimum threshold (&ge;65) get flagged for triage and posted straight to the <code>#career</code> Slack channel.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <span class="wf-connector" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </li>
        <li class="wf-node" style="--wf-accent: var(--doodle-pink, #FF1F70); --wf-ink: #FFFFFF;">
          <div class="wf-node-card">
            <div class="wf-node-top">
              <span class="wf-step-num">03</span>
              <span class="wf-node-tag">AI RESEARCH &middot; CULTURE FIT</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="wf-node-title">Checking company culture and fit</h3>
            <p class="wf-node-lead">For the jobs that pass the initial filter, an AI agent researches the company background, workplace reputation, and news to check for cultural red flags.</p>
            <button class="wf-expand-btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="wf-detail-03">
              <span class="wf-expand-label">Read the techy details</span>
              <span class="wf-chevron" aria-hidden="true">&#9662;</span>
            </button>
            <div class="wf-detail" id="wf-detail-03" hidden>
              <p class="wf-detail-p">A one-shot cron spins up an isolated Cordy (Claude) agent session. Cordy queries search tools to crawl engineering blogs, recent news, forums, and employee reviews. It compares findings against <code>job_ideals.md</code> (my defined values, preferred projects, and red lines), computes a 1 to 10 vibe score, and automatically archives anything rated 3 or lower.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <span class="wf-connector" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </li>
        <li class="wf-node" style="--wf-accent: var(--doodle-purple, #7A00FF); --wf-ink: #FFFFFF;">
          <div class="wf-node-card">
            <div class="wf-node-top">
              <span class="wf-step-num">04</span>
              <span class="wf-node-tag">LOCAL DASHBOARD &middot; REVIEW</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="wf-node-title">Reviewing matches in Mission Control</h3>
            <p class="wf-node-lead">Qualified roles appear on a private local dashboard where I can quickly review match reasons and choose whether to proceed.</p>
            <button class="wf-expand-btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="wf-detail-04">
              <span class="wf-expand-label">Read the techy details</span>
              <span class="wf-chevron" aria-hidden="true">&#9662;</span>
            </button>
            <div class="wf-detail" id="wf-detail-04" hidden>
              <p class="wf-detail-p">Mission Control runs locally on <code>localhost</code>, powered by SQLite. It provides an instant, keyboard-driven UI to inspect match breakdowns, salary data, and company research notes. Clicking <strong>Yes</strong> marks the row as <code>approved</code> in SQLite and immediately dispatches a tailoring event.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <span class="wf-connector" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </li>
        <li class="wf-node" style="--wf-accent: var(--doodle-cyan, #00B3E3); --wf-ink: #000000;">
          <div class="wf-node-card">
            <div class="wf-node-top">
              <span class="wf-step-num">05</span>
              <span class="wf-node-tag">TAILORED CV &middot; JOB MATCH</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="wf-node-title">Drafting a targeted CV</h3>
            <p class="wf-node-lead">When I approve a role, an AI agent drafts a CV tailored directly to the job description, without making up false experience.</p>
            <button class="wf-expand-btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="wf-detail-05">
              <span class="wf-expand-label">Read the techy details</span>
              <span class="wf-chevron" aria-hidden="true">&#9662;</span>
            </button>
            <div class="wf-detail" id="wf-detail-05" hidden>
              <p class="wf-detail-p">Approving a role schedules a one-shot cron (+15 seconds) that wakes Cordy in an isolated environment. Cordy analyzes the full job description and structures a targeted markdown draft. Content is strictly anchored to <code>master_cv.md</code>, ensuring factual accuracy while tailoring bullet points directly to the role requirements.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <span class="wf-connector" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </li>
        <li class="wf-node" style="--wf-accent: var(--doodle-yellow, #FFDA00); --wf-ink: #000000;">
          <div class="wf-node-card">
            <div class="wf-node-top">
              <span class="wf-step-num">06</span>
              <span class="wf-node-tag">HUMAN REVIEW &middot; PDF COMPILE</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="wf-node-title">Reviewing and compiling the PDF</h3>
            <p class="wf-node-lead">I inspect the drafted CV in markdown, make any desired tweaks which the agent remembers for future drafts, and generate a styled PDF with one click.</p>
            <button class="wf-expand-btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="wf-detail-06">
              <span class="wf-expand-label">Read the techy details</span>
              <span class="wf-chevron" aria-hidden="true">&#9662;</span>
            </button>
            <div class="wf-detail" id="wf-detail-06" hidden>
              <p class="wf-detail-p">The draft opens in Mission Control for human review. Any edits submitted back into the interface update <code>CORDELIA.md</code> prompt guidelines so the agent learns preferences over time. Clicking generate triggers a headless script that compiles the markdown through an HTML/CSS print template into a clean, recruiter-ready PDF.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
          <span class="wf-connector" aria-hidden="true"></span>
        </li>

        <!-- Outro: was a footnote under the chain, now the closing card of the
             chain itself, on desktop as well as mobile. -->
        <li class="wf-node wf-node-outro is-last" style="--wf-accent: #A1A1AA; --wf-ink: #000000;">
          <div class="wf-node-card">
            <div class="wf-node-top">
              <span class="wf-step-num">07</span>
              <span class="wf-node-tag">MANUAL SUBMIT &middot; QUALITY CHECK</span>
            </div>
            <h3 class="wf-node-title">Nothing is submitted for me</h3>
            <p class="wf-node-lead">
              I upload the compiled CV and submit the application myself. Keeping this manual guarantees total quality control and keeps me accountable for every application sent.<span class="wf-readme-sentence">
              For more information, open the
              <button class="wf-readme-link" type="button" id="wfReadmeLink">browser</button>
              in the interactive desktop.</span>
            </p>
            <button class="wf-expand-btn" type="button" aria-expanded="false" aria-controls="wf-detail-07">
              <span class="wf-expand-label">Read the techy details</span>
              <span class="wf-chevron" aria-hidden="true">&#9662;</span>
            </button>
            <div class="wf-detail" id="wf-detail-07" hidden>
              <p class="wf-detail-p">Automating the final submission creates significant risks: bot-detection bans, botched form parsing, and hallucinated answers to custom screening questions. Halting the workflow before submission protects recruiter trust, maintains 100% human accountability, and still saves over 80% of application time.</p>
            </div>
          </div>
        </li>
      </ol>

      <!-- Carousel position indicator. Mobile only; built and driven by
           initWorkflowCarousel() so it always matches the number of steps. -->
      <div class="wf-swipe-nav" hidden>
        <button class="wf-swipe-arrow" type="button" data-wf-prev aria-label="Previous step">&#8249;</button>
        <div class="wf-swipe-dots" data-wf-dots></div>
        <button class="wf-swipe-arrow" type="button" data-wf-next aria-label="Next step">&#8250;</button>
      </div>
    </div>
  </section>

</section>

<style>
  /* ---------------------------------------------------- */
  /* MASTER SECTION & SCROLLYTELLING RUNWAY               */
